In C programming, you can terminate a program using the `exit()` function from the standard library. This function causes the program to terminate immediately, and it can optionally return a status to the operating system. Here's how you can use it:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>  // Include the header for exit()

int main() {
    // Your program logic here

    // Terminate the program
    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);  // Use EXIT_FAILURE to indicate an error
}
```

